{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "This is the fromager repository (Python wheel builder). A virtualenv with the project\nand test dependencies is already set up at `.venv`; run tests with\n`.venv/bin/python -m pytest -o addopts=\"\" tests/...`.\n\nBug report:\n\n> With `--max-release-age` in multi-version bootstrap mode, a package that is pinned in\n> the constraints file (for example `boto3==1.35.88`) to a version older than the age\n> window has every candidate removed by the age filter and resolution fails silently.\n> In single-version mode the fallback keeps all candidates anyway, but logs a misleading\n> \"keeping all to avoid empty resolution\" warning for a package the user explicitly\n> pinned.\n>\n> A constraint is explicit user intent. Packages that have a constraint in the provider's\n> constraints object should skip age filtering entirely in\n> `find_all_matching_from_provider()` (see `src/fromager/resolver.py`), and log at INFO\n> level on the `fromager.resolver` logger:\n> `\"<name>: skipping age filter for constrained package (<N> candidate(s))\"`.\n> Unconstrained packages keep the current behaviour.\n\nFix it, update the docstring, add tests in `tests/test_cooldown.py` for both the\nconstrained and the unconstrained case, and run that test file."}, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T16:54:06.698Z"}
